{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC2 — H2 (reconciler echo loop) tested EXPERIMENTALLY. Result: NOT the producer, and no autonomous loop exists.\n\nRun in the existing real-git + real-CLI harness with the stateful Jira fake from\n`test_reconcile_idempotency.py` (the `robe-creek-zealot` harness, as required). New file:\n`tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_echo_loop_experiment.py` — 8 observational tests.\n**No production Jira, no production store.** Starting from a bound rebar↔Jira pair, each\nperturbation was followed by repeated passes recording ticket count, issue count, bindings\nand write-calls.\n\n| # | Perturbation | Local | Jira | Bounded? | What stopped it |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| a | binding dropped, `rebar-id:` label KEPT | 1→1 | 1→1 | yes, zero growth | `dispatch_one.py:154` dedup JQL hits → `dedup-create-skipped` + `bind_confirm`; zero Jira writes. Adopt arm stands down at `binding_walk.py:405-411` |\n| b | label removed, binding KEPT | 1→1 | 1→1 | yes, total no-op | `outbound_differ.py:588` keys create-vs-update solely off the binding; adopt skips bound keys (`binding_walk.py:202`) |\n| c | BOTH removed | 1→1 | 1→1 | yes | Deterministic id (`inbound_translate.py:93-97`) re-derives the SAME `jira-dig-1`, so re-adoption lands in the existing dir |\n| d | create-then-crash / outbound orphan (binding dropped + label stripped) | 2→**3** | 2→**3** | **bounded: +1/+1 in ONE pass** | Both new entities are bound and labelled in that same pass |\n| e | DC index lag + binding re-stripped EVERY pass | 2→2 | 2→**6** (+1/pass) | **unbounded WHILE FORCED** | Nothing — but this requires an external agent to re-break the binding every pass; it is not self-sustaining |\n| e2 | keyless-pending INSIDE 3600s grace + index lag | 2→2 | 2→2 | yes, zero growth | `dispatch_one.py:148-152` `is_keyless_pending_within_grace` defers the create |\n| e3 | keyless-pending PAST grace + index lag | 2→2 | 2→**3** | **bounded: +1** | Grace lifts, dedup JQL misses, one duplicate; its key is then bound so subsequent passes take the update branch |\n\n### Findings\n\n1. **There is no autonomous echo loop.** Every perturbation converges within one pass once\n   the perturbation stops. The unbounded case (e) is unbounded only while something keeps\n   re-breaking the binding on every pass — that is a driven process, not a loop.\n2. **The worst self-contained case is +1 local / +1 Jira, once** (d). It cannot produce 425.\n3. **Confirms the id-namespace discriminator empirically.** Seeding\n   `['ABC-42','DIG-1','DIG-2','proj-7']` produced `['jira-abc-42','jira-dig-1','jira-dig-2','jira-proj-7']`;\n   locally-authored tickets in the same store got canonical 4-quads. So an echo-created ticket\n   is **structurally distinguishable**. In the real store, **0 of 495** burst-window creates are\n   `jira-*` and all 40 `jira-*` tickets ever predate the burst (06-29..08-24). H2's contribution\n   to this incident is **zero**.\n\n### Reconciling with `robe-creek-zealot`\n\nNo contradiction to explain away. That ticket's \"dedup-skip prevents duplicate Jira issues\"\nis **reproduced exactly** by perturbation (a): with the `rebar-id:` label intact, the dedup JQL\nhits and nothing is created. Duplicates appear only when the LABEL is also gone (d/e3), which\nis the `nonmystic-topiary-toadfish` / `21fc-51d7-90ca-4a03` case — and even then the growth is\n+1 and bounded, consistent with those tickets rather than in tension with them.\n\n### Latent risks worth their own tickets (NOT this incident's cause)\n\n- **(e3) is real and reachable in production**: DC index lag past the keyless-pending grace\n  yields one duplicate Jira issue per affected ticket. This is `21fc-51d7-90ca-4a03`'s\n  mechanism, now reproduced in a harness.\n- **Harness defect (fake only, not production):** `binding_recovery.py:343-350` falls back to\n  the legacy hyphen JQL `labels = \"rebar-id-<id>\"`; `_FakeClient.search_issues` special-cases\n  only the colon form, so the hyphen query is answered as a WINDOW search returning every open\n  issue, and recovery then binds `results[0][\"key\"]` — mis-binding a pending local to an\n  unrelated key. Real JQL label-equality cannot do this, so it is a fake artifact, but it will\n  mislead any future test that exercises keyless-pending recovery.\n- **Accidental backstop:** in these runs `applier.py:592-600` (cross-project guard) aborted a\n  pass fail-closed only because the fake's project is `DIG` while configured scope is `REB`. In\n  a same-project deployment that guard would not fire.\n- **(c) leaves a duplicate CREATE event inside an existing ticket dir** — invisible to any\n  detector that counts directories or issues. Relevant to AC7 detector design."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788638920319473001,"uuid":"ff6fb6de-9773-45d7-bef3-88db5a5b6b35"}